    "text": "To find the length of the paint trail left by the tennis ball, we need to compute the arc length of the parametric curve given by \\((x(t), y(t)) = (3t^2 - 9t - 5, t^2 - 3t + 2)\\) for \\(0 \\le t \\le 4\\).\n\nThe formula for the arc length \\(L\\) of a parametric curve \\((x(t), y(t))\\) from \\(t = a\\) to \\(t = b\\) is given by:\n\\[\nL = \\int_a^b \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{dx}{dt}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{dy}{dt}\\right)^2} \\, dt\n\\]\n\nFirst, we need to find the derivatives \\(\\frac{dx}{dt}\\) and \\(\\frac{dy}{dt}\\).\n\nStarting with \\(x(t) = 3t^2 - 9t - 5\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{dx}{dt} = \\frac{d}{dt}(3t^2 - 9t - 5) = 6t - 9\n\\]\n\nNext, for \\(y(t) = t^2 - 3t + 2\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{dy}{dt} = \\frac{d}{dt}(t^2 - 3t + 2) = 2t - 3\n\\]\n\nNow, we compute \\(\\left(\\frac{dx}{dt}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{dy}{dt}\\right)^2\\):\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{dx}{dt}\\right)^2 = (6t - 9)^2 = 36t^2 - 108t + 81\n\\]\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{dy}{dt}\\right)^2 = (2t - 3)^2 = 4t^2 - 12t + 9\n\\]\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{dx}{dt}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{dy}{dt}\\right)^2 = 36t^2 - 108t + 81 + 4t^2 - 12t + 9 = 40t^2 - 120t + 90\n\\]\n\nThe arc length integral becomes:\n\\[\nL = \\int_0^4 \\sqrt{40t^2 - 120t + 90} \\, dt\n\\]\n\nTo simplify the integrand, we factor out the constant from the square root:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{40t^2 - 120t + 90} = \\sqrt{10(4t^2 - 12t + 9)} = \\sqrt{10(2t - 3)^2} = \\sqrt{10} |2t - 3|\n\\]\n\nSince \\(0 \\le t \\le 4\\), the expression \\(2t - 3\\) is non-negative for \\(t \\ge \\frac{3}{2}\\) and non-positive for \\(t \\le \\frac{3}{2}\\). Therefore, we split the integral into two parts:\n\\[\nL = \\sqrt{10} \\left( \\int_0^{\\frac{3}{2}} -(2t - 3) \\, dt + \\int_{\\frac{3}{2}}^4 (2t - 3) \\, dt \\right)\n\\]\n\nEvaluate the first integral:\n\\[\n\\int_0^{\\frac{3}{2}} -(2t - 3) \\, dt = \\int_0^{\\frac{3}{2}} (-2t + 3) \\, dt = \\left[ -t^2 + 3t \\right]_0^{\\frac{3}{2}} = \\left( -\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2 + 3 \\cdot \\frac{3}{2} \\right) - (0) = -\\frac{9}{4} + \\frac{9}{2} = \\frac{9}{4}\n\\]\n\nEvaluate the second integral:\n\\[\n\\int_{\\frac{3}{2}}^4 (2t - 3) \\, dt = \\left[ t^2 - 3t \\right]_{\\frac{3}{2}}^4 = \\left( 4^2 - 3 \\cdot 4 \\right) - \\left( \\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2 - 3 \\cdot \\frac{3}{2} \\right) = (16 - 12) - \\left( \\frac{9}{4} - \\frac{9}{2} \\right) = 4 - \\left( \\frac{9}{4} - \\frac{18}{4} \\right) = 4 + \\frac{9}{4} = \\frac{16}{4} + \\frac{9}{4} = \\frac{25}{4}\n\\]\n\nCombine the results:\n\\[\nL = \\sqrt{10} \\left( \\frac{9}{4} + \\frac{25}{4} \\right) = \\sqrt{10} \\left( \\frac{34}{4} \\right) = \\sqrt{10} \\cdot \\frac{17}{2} = \\frac{17\\sqrt{10}}{2}\n\\]\n\nThus, the length of the paint trail is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{17\\sqrt{10}}{2}}\n\\]",
